# Git cannot store an empty directory, and this directory being EMPTY is the point.
#
# The attacker is handed an empty exploit/ and submitted-bypass/ to write into, and the
# fs-sandbox isolation check verifies both are present and writable. Without this file a
# fresh clone has no such directories, the check fails, and every package-backed family
# drops from adversarial-ready to audit-pending -- on CI only, on a machine that had never
# run .
